From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:45:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 030/105] gdn: strided q/k/v read at the full T=16 tile (patch
 for the vendored WY wrapper)

The vendored FlashInfer WY output-only wrapper .contiguous()-materialises q/k/v at
T == T_KERNEL, which is three gmem->gmem copies per GDN layer (108 kernels /
~200 us per W16 decode step, measured in prof/traces/gemv3b-w16-code-edit).  They
exist only because the kernel's descriptor assumed a compact token stride, but the
kernel reads q/k/v through raw base pointers plus strides it rebuilds itself, and it
already has a `qkv_row_stride` knob used by the T in {4,8} native path.

At T == T_KERNEL n_valid == T, so the plain (no smem-tail-zeroing) path runs and the
only thing that changes is the gmem address arithmetic: the same values are read
straight out of the fused conv-output column slices (token stride conv_dim = 10240
for this model, features contiguous within a token).

Delivered as bench/glue_e/gdn_wy_T16_strided.patch rather than an in-place edit: the
file lives in the venv and a running server re-imports it.  The patch also tightens
the guard (shared token stride, canonical head/feature/batch strides, 16 B alignment)
and reuses it for the pre-existing native path, where it can only fall back to the
copies, never change a result.

test/srt/layers/test_gdn_wy_t16_strided.py applies the patch to a temp copy, imports
it beside the installed module and proves bit-identical output at T=16 and T=4 on
the real shapes (H=HK=16x128, HV=48x128, conv_dim 10240), plus a compile-cache probe
so a silent fallback cannot make the bit-identity vacuous.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
